nodecode-eventforge is a rewrite of sinequix's sinequix/eventforge:

  https://github.com/sinequix/eventforge
  commit 1b556629b6a20d1f8194beaab8c38253cd837c64
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 EventForge contributors (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's whole client surface against one EventForge control
plane — ef_list_events (GET /events, with a payload trusted only when its
signature was verified and otherwise withheld or wrapped as untrusted data),
ef_emit_event (POST /events), ef_query_memory (GET /memory), 
ef_list_pending_actions (GET /actions, the pending proposals with their
proposal text, risk and expiry, oldest first), ef_approve_action
(POST /actions/{id}/decision), ef_list_workflows (GET /workflows),
ef_spawn_subagent (POST /agent-runs), ef_forge_mcp (POST /forge),
ef_approve_forge (POST /forge/{id}/decision) and ef_listen_for_webhook
(POST /relay/ensure), with their argument schemas, their workspace and
project scoping, the UUID rule on every id a request path carries, and the
/eventforge status, events and replay command — the last a read-only view of
one stored event with the runs, action proposals and audit lines its id
correlates. The Python (urllib, dataclasses, a per-call settings read) is
Common Lisp here: nlk:http for the plane's routes, one section declaration
for the settings, ten nlk:define-contract declarations for the tools'
arguments, and a :tool hook in place of the plugin's post_tool_call hook,
which writes the same one-line audit record ("<tool> ok in 12ms") into the
plane's own /audit log without the call's arguments or its answer. The base
URL rule is the plugin's: an absolute http(s) URL, plain http only on
loopback, no credentials inside it, and the bearer token read from one
environment variable and sent nowhere else.

Left out: pre_llm_call, the hook that pushed newly verified events into the
next model request's context, because a cell contributes to a turn through
:tool and :frame hooks and the frame composer, not through a Hermes hook
named for its own request; the same facts are a call away in ef_list_events,
which the manual tells the model to make. pre_tool_call's approval gate is
left out too: it asked Hermes to prompt a person before the four
irreversible tools, where a cell states the same thing in each tool's
description and leaves the prompt to the shell's own approval flow. The
auto_start half of bundle.py — spawning the repository's prebuilt
eventforge-standalone.cjs with node when /health was down — is not
reproduced, because a cell does not bundle another product's executable:
run the control plane yourself, or point the section at one already running.
The read-only triage skill (skills/triage/SKILL.md) is folded into the
manual the tools carry, since it taught the model to walk the same routes
the tools already expose.
